{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:BringsSurface.BriggsKleinChart","@type":"LeanModule","name":"BringsSurface.BriggsKleinChart","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:Mathlib.Algebra.Polynomial.Laurent","lean:module:Mathlib.Data.Int.Basic","lean:module:Mathlib.Data.Complex.Basic","lean:module:Mathlib.Analysis.SpecialFunctions.Complex.Circle"],"declarations":14,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Brings.c5_preserves_normSq","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Brings.c5_preserves_normSq","kind":"theorem","line":67,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/brings-surface/briggs-klein-chart.lean#L67-L77","doc":"The radial coordinate r = |w₁|² is C₅-invariant:\n|ζᵏ w₁|² = |ζᵏ|² · |w₁|² = 1 · |w₁|² = |w₁|².\nHere we express this for the normSq function. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Brings.c5_phase_rotation","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Brings.c5_phase_rotation","kind":"def","line":61,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/brings-surface/briggs-klein-chart.lean#L61-L65","doc":"The C₅ phase rotation on the k-th coordinate: ζᵏ · w.\nSince ζ⁵ = 1, the action is periodic with period 5. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Brings.zeta_angle","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Brings.zeta_angle","kind":"def","line":57,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/brings-surface/briggs-klein-chart.lean#L57-L59","doc":"Primitive 5th root of unity phase angle. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Brings.c5_order","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Brings.c5_order","kind":"def","line":53,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/brings-surface/briggs-klein-chart.lean#L53-L55","doc":"The C₅ action order: the cyclic group acting by phase rotation. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Brings.BriggsKleinChart.r_pos","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Brings.BriggsKleinChart.r_pos","kind":"theorem","line":51,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/brings-surface/briggs-klein-chart.lean#L51-L51","doc":"The chart is restricted to 0 < r. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Brings.BriggsKleinChart.r_eq","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Brings.BriggsKleinChart.r_eq","kind":"theorem","line":49,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/brings-surface/briggs-klein-chart.lean#L49-L49","doc":"r is the squared modulus of w₁. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Brings.BriggsKleinChart.r","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Brings.BriggsKleinChart.r","kind":"def","line":47,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/brings-surface/briggs-klein-chart.lean#L47-L47","doc":"Radial coordinate r = |w₁|². ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Brings.BriggsKleinChart.w₂","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Brings.BriggsKleinChart.w₂","kind":"def","line":45,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/brings-surface/briggs-klein-chart.lean#L45-L45","doc":"Second resolvent coordinate w₂ ∈ ℂ. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Brings.BriggsKleinChart.w₁","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Brings.BriggsKleinChart.w₁","kind":"def","line":43,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/brings-surface/briggs-klein-chart.lean#L43-L43","doc":"First resolvent coordinate w₁ ∈ ℂ. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Brings.BriggsKleinChart.mk","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Brings.BriggsKleinChart.mk","kind":"ctor","line":41,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/brings-surface/briggs-klein-chart.lean#L41-L41","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Brings.BriggsKleinChart","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Brings.BriggsKleinChart","kind":"structure","line":32,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/brings-surface/briggs-klein-chart.lean#L32-L51","doc":"**Briggs–Klein affine chart**: coordinate system on Bring's surface\nusing resolvent coordinates (w₁, w₂) ∈ ℂ², restricted to the open\nset where the radial coordinate r = |w₁|² satisfies 0 < r < ∞.\n\nThe C₅ cyclic group acts by phase rotation w_k ↦ ζᵏ w_k, where\nζ = exp(2πi/5) is a primitive 5th root of unity. The radial\ncoordinate r is C₅-invariant.\n\nRef: [leitner2026] Chapter 5, §Bundle structures ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Brings.q_inv_param","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Brings.q_inv_param","kind":"def","line":30,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/brings-surface/briggs-klein-chart.lean#L30-L30","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Brings.q_param","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Brings.q_param","kind":"def","line":29,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/brings-surface/briggs-klein-chart.lean#L29-L29","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Brings.R_q","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Brings.R_q","kind":"def","line":26,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/brings-surface/briggs-klein-chart.lean#L26-L28","doc":"Ground ring `R_q = ℤ[q, q⁻¹]` (Laurent polynomials over ℤ).\nSee `QOU.Archimedean.GroundRing` for the compiled definition. ","signatureChunk":0}]}